# Fixture registry: two types the fixture source does not write, classified differently, so one assertion
# separates the two risks. `Ghost` is the graveyard entry the staleness check exists against and must be
# reported; `Phantom` is uncarried for the ordinary reason a person type is — its literal would live in the
# constant its own owner holds — and must NOT be, or the check goes back to being satisfied by the very
# declaration it verifies.
#
# The paths on the person line are shaped like real ones but are never resolved: the erasure-owner rule is
# pinned against the real tree, where a file that genuinely fails to erase exists to point at.
FixtureResource => non-person
Ghost => non-person
Phantom => person :: src/Fixture/PhantomEraser.php :: features/witness-complete.feature
